    "description": "Cancel a queued or running job; for remote jobs this cancels the underlying A2A task too. Already-finished jobs are returned unchanged. Use job_retry to run a cancelled job again. A job running on another instance is stopped by its own instance shortly after, so the job comes back still \`running\` and reaches \`cancelled\` within a few seconds — poll job_get rather than assuming the returned state is final.",
